A Samurai dual-wielding +7 Excalibur and a +7 katana does much the same,
with the added minor bonus of being able to windshield liches where your
rogue will have trouble. (since liches do not take silver damage and are
immune to life drain, thus making both your weapons materially inferior
to the Samurai's weapons.)

It is generally the case that most characters can windshield most
monsters in the late game, due to the ludicrously overwhelming impact of
Luck on the player's to-hit rolls and the fact that monster armour class
peaks at about -10 or so, which is largely irrelevant when the player
has +20 or more to hit plus the dice-skewing effects of maxed Luck.

Two-weaponing, of course, just makes this worse.  The sacrifice (no
shield for you!) is not enough of a penalty now that we have silver DSM,
allowing the player (without using artifacts) to have reflection, magic
resistance, brilliance, extrinsic telepathy, and both hands free for
weapons, given the ludicrous advantage provided by having two weapons.
